<p>
    The Code 128 barcode is a high-density linear barcode symbology that can encode alphanumeric characters.
    It is widely used in various industries for inventory management, shipping, and product labeling due to its compact size and ability to encode a large amount of data.
    The <code>Code128Symbology</code> component can be used to generate Code 128 barcodes in your application.
    It contains 4 parameters :

    <ul>
        <li><code>ModuleHeight</code> : Height of the bars</li>
        <li><code>ModuleWidth</code> : Width of a bar</li>
        <li><code>ShowText</code> : Show the raw encoded text.</li>
        <li><code>Subset</code> : Allow the user to specify the subset to use for encoding.</li>
    </ul>

    The subset parameter allows you to specify which subset of the Code 128 symbology to use. The options are:
    A : Uppercase letters, numbers, and special characters
    B : Uppercase and lowercase letters, numbers, and special characters
    C : Numeric characters only
</p>

<div style="height: 400px">
    <FluentStack Height="100%" VerticalGap="50" Orientation="Orientation.Vertical">
        <FluentTextInput Immediate
                         Label="Value to encode as barcode"
                         @bind-Value="Value" />
        
        <FluentCxBarcode Value="@Value">
            <Code128Symbology />
        </FluentCxBarcode>
    </FluentStack>
</div>

@code {
    private string Value { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
